{"id":"bp05","name":"Sensor Grid Counts","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["garden"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A greenhouse is mapped as a rectangular grid <code>garden</code>. Each string is one row: <code>'*'</code> is a plant with a sensor alert, and <code>' '</code> is an empty cell.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the same grid where every empty cell is replaced by the number of alert cells among its <b>8 neighbours</b> (horizontal, vertical and diagonal). If an empty cell has no alert neighbour, it stays <code>' '</code>. Alert cells stay <code>'*'</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>garden = [\" * \", \"   \", \"** \"]</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[\"1*1\", \"332\", \"**1\"]</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.string garden<br><b>[output]</b> array.string</div>","starter":"def solution(garden):\n    # write your code here\n    return garden\n","hints":["Pour chaque case, parcours dr et dc dans (-1, 0, 1) en sautant (0, 0), et vérifie que la voisine est dans la grille.","Attention aux lignes vides : la grille peut avoir des lignes mais 0 colonne."],"summary_fr":"Dans une grille, chaque case vide reçoit le nombre de * parmi ses 8 voisines (rien si 0). Les * restent des *.","tags":["grille","8 voisins","bornes"],"minutes":15,"source":"exercism/problem-specifications (MIT) · flower-field","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"garden":[" * ","   ","** "]},"expected":{"value":["1*1","332","**1"]}},{"input":{"garden":["*  *"]},"expected":{"value":["*11*"]}}],"hidden_n":16,"hidden":"","solution":""}